PUT api/[controller]/product/preparing/{idproduct}
PUT controller responsible for setting an item order to Preparing status
The order ID that belongs to the product. The product ID to be updated. An ActionResult containing a Json Object and the message.

PUT api/[controller]/product/ready/{productId}
PUT controller responsible for setting an item order to Ready status
THe order ID that belongs to the product. The product ID to be updated. An ActionResult containing a Json Object and the message.

PUT api/[controller]/product/ready/{productId}
PUT controller responsible for setting an item order to Cancelled status
The order ID that belongs to the product. The product ID to be updated. An ActionResult containing a Json Object and the message.

PUT api/[controller]/product/preparing/{productId}

PUT controller responsible for setting an order to ready after all products are ready.

The order ID to be updated to Ready state.

 POST api/[controller]/placeorders

 Endpoint responsible to process multiple order requests.


 Usage Example:

[
  {
    "PosId": 1,
     "Items": [
     {
     "Id": 1,
     "Name": "Burger",
     "Status": 1,
     "KitchenArea": 1
     }
     ],
     "Status": 1 
  },
  {
    "PosId": 1,
    "Items": [
      {
        "Id": 1,
        "Name": "Fries",
        "Status": 1,
        "KitchenArea": 2
      },
      {
        "Id": 2,
        "Name": "Burger",
        "Status": 1,
        "KitchenArea": 1
      }
    ],
    "Status": 1 
  },
]


 The list of orders to be inserted. It must be a Json Array.
 An ActionResult containing a Json Object and the message.

PUT api/[controller]/order/cancel/{orderId}
PUT controller responsible for setting an order to Cancelled status
The order ID to be cancelled. An ActionResult containing a Json Object and the message.
